  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "We replace $x$ with $18$ in the given expression, and simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{x+6} & = \\\\ \\sqrt{18+6} & = \\\\ \\sqrt{24}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can simplify even further using the product rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{24} & = \\\\ \\sqrt{4\\cdot 6} & = \\\\ \\sqrt{{2}^{2}\\cdot 6} & = \\\\ \\sqrt{{2}^{2}}\\cdot \\sqrt{6} & = \\\\ 2\\sqrt{6}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
